an></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2999501252">October 7, 2019</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">I wasn’t expecting Ella to have her own story as she was very much a background character but I’m certainly glad she did. This book really is the last book in the series and centres around Ella and Jake. Ella was not only with the Koa Point shifters in the military but she was also the foster sister of Kai and Hunter and whilst Jake is human, his military unit also served with the shifter’s unit so they know he is as tough as is humanly possible. What they don’t know however, is that Ella and Jake had one night of passion the previous year in which Jake fell in love and Ella learnt that he was her mate! A mate Ella tells herself she can’t have because of him being unlikely to survive the transition into shifter.<br /><br />The story starts with the shifters needing extra security at Koa Point and especially with the upcoming nuptials of Silas and Cassandra at the upmarket Kapa’akea Resort… a necessity since Silas was the most eligible bachelor on Maui and so they ask Ella to return to the estate, which she does with no questions asked. They also offer Jake some work as part of their security team and both he and Ella are thrust together again which causes them both emotional angst. Just when Ella thinks it can’t get any worse, Kai also comes up with the undercover story of Ella and Jake being on their honeymoon at the resort so they can stake it out security wise. <br />Because she can’t think of a valid reason why they shouldn’t, Ella finds herself ‘married’ to her mate whilst still trying to rebuff him. For his part, Jake is only left confused by Ella blowing hot and cold but being ever the gentlemen that he is, he lets Ella call the shots. In the meantime, he is trying to work out what is happening to the guys in his former military unit since they left the service and whether it will impact on him.<br /><br />We learn that Moira is still obsessed with the Koa Point shifters hence the reason for the extra security, we meet a new and rather unusual shifter and Nina has her twins… which bizarrely leads to a make or break time for Ella and Jake.<br /><br />I am voluntarily reviewing this book, gifted to me by the author with no obligation.<br /><br /><br /></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/13055353?shelf=contemporary" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">contemporary</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/13055353?shelf=dragons" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">dragons</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/13055353?shelf=hea" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">hea</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium" aria-label="Show all items in the list"><span class="Button__labelItem">...more</span></button></div></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,