33 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4589612992">March 5, 2022</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Oh my gosh, Ella is so adorable. My heart broke for her, as a female shifter she has it so much harder than the men. Her feisty yet very stubborn attitude is extremely refreshing, she's a woman who can hold her own. Then there's Jake, now he is absolutely gorgeous. Everything about him makes me swoon, he's strong, determined and a little unsure of himself when it comes to Ella. The two of them end of in several awkward predicaments, which had me rolling over laughing at their rotten luck. The way both of them tripped over each other, metaphorically speaking. There's also the rest of the guys, the constant teasing was so good. The storyline is really fun and exciting, exactly what I've come to love about Anna Lowe's books. All of her characters are interesting and different, I love every single one of them. It's very hard to pick a favourite because they all are amazing, and the way she describes the places sounds so incredible. Coha point really makes you wish you were there, sorry if I misspelled that. Between the way everything is described and switching perspectives, these are what I love so much with the authors writing. This series is absolutely amazing, the narrator does a wonderful job reading this beautiful story.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button ty